  "refusal.section.thisSolidIsMeshOnly": "this solid is mesh-only (a general boolean's result, OP-9), so its section has no faces to name — its curves draw as chords and cannot be used as construction inputs; build the geometry you want to anchor on from the operands' own sketches instead",
  "@refusal.section.thisSolidIsMeshOnly": {
    "description": "Refusal message of ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program that builds geometry as a dependency graph (a construction, not a constraint solver). It is shown in the status line and beside the element in the side panel, to say why something the user asked for cannot be built and what to do instead. This one is about naming, sectioning and reading the faces and edges of a solid.",
